   "end": 566.66,
   "text": "of"
  },
  {
   "t": 566.66,
   "end": 567.22,
   "text": "consciousness"
  },
  {
   "t": 567.22,
   "end": 568.84,
   "text": "this is"
  },
  {
   "t": 568.84,
   "end": 568.98,
   "text": "the"
  },
  {
   "t": 568.98,
   "end": 569.3,
   "text": "meaning"
  },
  {
   "t": 569.3,
   "end": 569.52,
   "text": "of"
  },
  {
   "t": 569.52,
   "end": 570.3,
   "text": "kasvarata"
  },
  {
   "t": 570.3,
   "end": 571.18,
   "text": "resonance"
  },
  {
   "t": 571.18,
   "end": 571.7,
   "text": "of the"
  },
  {
   "t": 571.7,
   "end": 571.98,
   "text": "void"
  },
  {
   "t": 573.12,
   "end": 574.04,
   "text": "at the"
  },
  {
   "t": 574.04,
   "end": 574.44,
   "text": "end"
  },
  {
   "t": 574.44,
   "end": 575.2,
   "text": "anandosha"
  },
  {
   "t": 575.2,
   "end": 575.68,
   "text": "divider"
  },
  {
   "t": 575.68,
   "end": 576.46,
   "text": "sums up"
  },
  {
   "t": 576.46,
   "end": 577.16,
   "text": "and gives"
  },
  {
   "t": 577.16,
   "end": 577.92,
   "text": "an overview"
  },
  {
   "t": 577.92,
   "end": 578.68,
   "text": "of the"
  },
  {
   "t": 578.68,
   "end": 579.08,
   "text": "entire"
  },
  {
   "t": 579.08,
   "end": 579.48,
   "text": "text"
  },
  {
   "t": 579.48,
   "end": 580.42,
   "text": "or other"
  },
  {
   "t": 580.42,
   "end": 580.92,
   "text": "oral"
  },
  {
   "t": 580.92,
   "end": 581.86,
   "text": "transmission"
  },
  {
   "t": 582.64,
   "end": 583.58,
   "text": "back to"
  },
  {
   "t": 583.58,
   "end": 583.72,
   "text": "the"
  },
  {
   "t": 583.72,
   "end": 584.1,
   "text": "quote"
  },
  {
   "t": 584.1,
   "end": 585.78,
   "text": "a certain"
  },
  {
   "t": 585.78,
   "end": 586.34,
   "text": "kaola"
  },
  {
   "t": 586.34,
   "end": 587.02,
   "text": "ascetic"
  },
  {
   "t": 587.02,
   "end": 587.78,
   "text": "arotuta"
  },
  {
   "t": 587.78,
   "end": 588.48,
   "text": "that is"
  },
  {
   "t": 588.48,
   "end": 589.28,
   "text": "vaturanata"
  },
  {
   "t": 589.28,
   "end": 590.76,
   "text": "has revealed"
  },
  {
   "t": 590.76,
   "end": 591.3,
   "text": "the oral"
  },
  {
   "t": 591.3,
   "end": 591.88,
   "text": "tradition"
  },
  {
   "t": 591.88,
   "end": 592.38,
   "text": "of the"
  },
  {
   "t": 592.38,
   "end": 592.7,
   "text": "time"
  },
  {
   "t": 592.7,
   "end": 593.2,
   "text": "of the"
  },
  {
   "t": 593.2,
   "end": 593.5,
   "text": "great"
  },
  {
   "t": 593.5,
   "end": 593.92,
   "text": "union"
  },
  {
   "t": 593.92,
   "end": 594.46,
   "text": "with the"
  },
  {
   "t": 594.46,
   "end": 595.06,
   "text": "goddesses"
  },
  {
   "t": 595.06,
   "end": 595.78,
   "text": "of the"
  },
  {
   "t": 595.78,
   "end": 596.26,
   "text": "sacred"
  },
  {
   "t": 596.26,
   "end": 596.76,
   "text": "seeds"
  },
  {
   "t": 596.76,
   "end": 597.82,
   "text": "piteshary"
  },
  {
   "t": 597.82,
   "end": 599.22,
   "text": "composed"
  },
  {
   "t": 599.22,
   "end": 599.78,
   "text": "in the"
  },
  {
   "t": 599.78,
   "end": 599.98,
   "text": "form"
  },
  {
   "t": 600.0,
   "end": 607.8,
   "text": "of sutras, by attaining direct experience of non-duality, of the plane of the Anuttara"
  },
  {
   "t": 607.8,
   "end": 614.86,
   "text": "in the oral teaching of the 13 sutras, which contain the essence of the six darshanals,"
  },
  {
   "t": 615.3,
   "end": 620.36,
   "text": "the four tantric traditions, and all the unions of Siddha and Yogini."
  },
  {
   "t": 621.36,
   "end": 628.0,
   "text": "On this I have composed a brief commentary in order to awaken the good and the wise."
  },
  {
   "t": 628.0,
   "end": 632.02,
   "text": "This is the motivation that Anandashat Dupada gives."
  },
  {
   "t": 632.5,
   "end": 639.24,
   "text": "The purpose of the commentary is to awaken the good, sad, and the wise."
  },
  {
   "t": 640.2,
   "end": 645.04,
   "text": "Then he concludes with a verse, Sankha Sotra."
  },
  {
   "t": 645.82,
   "end": 653.24,
   "text": "Somebody, that is what Unanatta, has perfectly and expressly revealed the supreme secret,"
  },
  {
   "t": 653.56,
   "end": 657.26,
   "text": "which is free from the mass of discursive thoughts of language."
  },
  {
   "t": 658.0,
   "end": 663.1,
   "text": "Being liberated from the error which separates worldly and divine reality,"
  },
  {
   "t": 663.8,
   "end": 672.2,
   "text": "incomparable by an expansion of consciousness in a mode which is a manifestation of the supreme reality,"
  },
  {
   "t": 672.66,
   "end": 679.72,
   "text": "of the great intensity, or suddenness, sahasa, which is partless and uncreated."
  },
  {
   "t": 679.72,
   "end": 681.7,
   "text": "End of the quote."
  },
  {
   "t": 684.44,
   "end": 692.38,
   "text": "The interpretation of this final sutra differs substantially between Anandashat Dupada and Swami Lakshman too."
  },
  {
   "t": 693.38,
   "end": 696.7,
   "text": "Swamiji's interpretation is clear and straightforward."
  },
  {
   "t": 696.7,
   "end": 701.78,
   "text": "Let us first listen to his translation of the sutra."
  },
  {
   "t": 702.68,
   "end": 703.52,
   "text": "Quote,"
  },
  {
   "t": 704.48,
   "end": 708.54,
   "text": "By maintaining the power of speechless state of speech,"
  },
  {
   "t": 708.72,
   "end": 709.26,
   "text": "Parav,"
  },
  {
   "t": 709.8,
   "end": 712.3,
   "text": "One attains the mutra of astonishment,"
  },
  {
   "t": 713.16,
   "end": 716.9,
   "text": "Hence, entry in the kingdom of voidness flows forth."
  },
  {
   "t": 718.68,
   "end": 723.8,
   "text": "He takes the negative prefix in Akatana only in the sense of speechless,"
  },
  {
   "t": 724.32,
   "end": 728.7,
   "text": "not related to the letter A, as says Anandashat Dupada."
  },
  {
   "t": 729.82,
   "end": 733.58,
   "text": "And he gives more importance to the mystical expression,"
  },
  {
   "t": 733.82,
   "end": 735.52,
   "text": "Maha Vismaya Buddha,"
  },
  {
   "t": 735.96,
   "end": 739.8,
   "text": "which is the key for understanding this concluding sutra."
  },
  {
   "t": 741.02,
   "end": 743.9,
   "text": "Swamiji relates Akatana-balena,"
  },
  {
   "t": 744.1,
   "end": 746.36,
   "text": "the power of speechless speech,"
  },
  {
   "t": 746.6,
   "end": 747.38,
   "text": "to Parav,"
  },
  {
   "t": 747.88,
   "end": 749.78,
   "text": "the supreme level of the word,"
  },
  {
   "t": 750.2,
   "end": 750.68,
   "text": "Parav."
  },
  {
   "t": 752.26,
   "end": 755.3,
   "text": "That Akatana-gata-balena means,"
  },
  {
   "t": 755.58,
   "end": 755.8,
   "text": "Quote,"
  },
  {
   "t": 756.3,
   "end": 759.2,
   "text": "That Akatana-gata-balena means,"
  },
  {
   "t": 759.42,
   "end": 762.86,
   "text": "by maintaining the power of speechless state of speech,"
  },
  {
   "t": 763.06,
   "end": 763.56,
   "text": "Parav,"
  },
  {
   "t": 764.74,
   "end": 768.24,
   "text": "One attains the mutra of the state of astonishment."
  },
  {
   "t": 769.8,
   "end": 772.94,
   "text": "In descending order after Parav follows Pashyati,"
  },
  {
   "t": 773.34,
   "end": 773.94,
   "text": "the visionary,"
  },
  {
   "t": 774.76,
   "end": 775.88,
   "text": "where there is no speech,"
  },
  {
   "t": 776.12,
   "end": 778.04,
   "text": "but a subtle tendency,"
  },
  {
   "t": 778.06,
   "end": 778.6,
   "text": "Quote,"
  },
  {
   "t": 779.1,
   "end": 781.86,
   "text": "towards the outward flow in the world of speech,"
  },
  {
   "t": 782.3,
   "end": 785.42,
   "text": "that is in the world of objectivity."
  },
  {
   "t": 786.46,
   "end": 788.42,
   "text": "The next stage is Matema,"
  },
  {
   "t": 789.14,
   "end": 792.42,
   "text": "the intermediate state of speech at the level of thought."
  },
  {
   "t": 793.98,
   "end": 796.24,
   "text": "The lowest English descent is Vikery,"
  },
  {
   "t": 796.24,
   "end": 800.0,
   "text": "the absolute cross form in Swamiji's words."
  },
  {
   "t": 800.66,
   "end": 804.16,
   "text": "The main difference between Matema and Vikery"
  },
  {
   "t": 804.16,
   "end": 807.92,
   "text": "is that Matema is internal cross speech"
  },
  {
   "t": 807.92,
   "end": 810.54,
   "text": "and later is external cross speech."
  },
  {
   "t": 812.02,
   "end": 816.9,
   "text": "He connects Mahavismaya Mudra with the Shira Sutra,"
  },
  {
   "t": 817.18,
   "end": 819.14,
   "text": "Visma-yo-yoga-pulmika,"
  },
  {
   "t": 819.62,
   "end": 823.3,
   "text": "the highest states of yoga are full of wonder."
  },
  {
   "t": 825.0,
   "end": 828.62,
   "text": "Now he explains the content of this wonder and surprise."
  },
  {
   "t": 829.32,
   "end": 829.94,
   "text": "Quote,"
  },
  {
   "t": 830.86,
   "end": 832.36,
   "text": "Visma-yoga-mutra means"
  },
  {
   "t": 832.36,
   "end": 833.88,
   "text": "the stand imprinted,"
  },
  {
   "t": 833.88,
   "end": 835.3,
   "text": "this is the meaning of mudra,"
  },
  {
   "t": 835.5,
   "end": 836.44,
   "text": "it's also a stand,"
  },
  {
   "t": 836.88,
   "end": 837.58,
   "text": "an imprint."
  },
  {
   "t": 838.38,
   "end": 841.92,
   "text": "The stand imprinted under Visma-yoga-leil astonishment."
  },
  {
   "t": 842.36,
   "end": 844.06,
   "text": "Because one is astonished."
  },
  {
   "t": 845.1,
   "end": 846.44,
   "text": "What for I was working?"
  },
  {
   "t": 846.86,
   "end": 849.1,
   "text": "What for I was doing practice of yoga?"
  },
  {
   "t": 849.48,
   "end": 852.7,
   "text": "What for I had discarded all the activities of the world?"
  },
  {
   "t": 853.06,
   "end": 855.74,
   "text": "What for I had gone to the feet of my master?"
  },
  {
   "t": 855.74,
   "end": 857.86,
   "text": "All what I feel now,"
  },
  {
   "t": 858.08,
   "end": 860.2,
   "text": "I was already feeling that."
  },
  {
   "t": 861.22,
   "end": 863.22,
   "text": "So he's filled with Visma-yoga,"
  },
  {
   "t": 863.4,
   "end": 864.34,
   "text": "with astonishment."
  },
  {
   "t": 866.22,
   "end": 869.0,
   "text": "There remains the equally mystical Kasvarata"
  },
  {
   "t": 869.0,
   "end": 871.3,
   "text": "on which he elaborates"
  },
  {
   "t": 871.3,
   "end": 874.44,
   "text": "taking Swamata in the sense of radiance,"
  },
  {
   "t": 874.94,
   "end": 875.52,
   "text": "not salt."
  },
  {
   "t": 876.58,
   "end": 877.38,
   "text": "Quote,"
  },
  {
   "t": 878.12,
   "end": 880.76,
   "text": "K means in the cheetah culture,"
  },
  {
   "t": 881.18,
   "end": 882.5,
   "text": "the sky of consciousness,"
  },
  {
   "t": 882.96,
   "end": 885.48,
   "text": "and Swamata means one's establishment,"
  },
  {
   "t": 885.74,
   "end": 887.58,
   "text": "in his own eternal nature,"
  },
  {
   "t": 887.94,
   "end": 890.02,
   "text": "of spontaneous radiance."
  },
  {
   "t": 890.44,
   "end": 892.82,
   "text": "That nature is nothing but void,"
  },
  {
   "t": 893.36,
   "end": 896.42,
   "text": "filled with universal God-consciousness."
  },
  {
   "t": 896.68,
   "end": 897.78,
   "text": "End of the quote."
  },
  {
   "t": 899.54,
   "end": 901.12,
   "text": "By trying to sum up"
  },
  {
   "t": 901.12,
   "end": 903.62,
   "text": "this highly mystical concluding Sutra,"
  },
  {
   "t": 904.2,
   "end": 906.58,
   "text": "one becomes equally speechless,"
  },
  {
   "t": 907.06,
   "end": 909.48,
   "text": "and lands in the great silence."
  },
  {
   "t": 909.48,
   "end": 909.72,
   "text": "with the"
  },
  {
   "t": 909.92,
   "end": 910.2,
   "text": "yss."
  },
  {
   "t": 922.66,
   "end": 924.38,
   "text": "Thank you."
  },
  {
   "t": 910.2,
   "end": 911.44,
   "text": "Thank you."
  }
 ]
}